# User Profile Example

Keep the real profile in `local-only/assistant/profile.md`.

This file describes stable user preferences and philosophy that the assistant should remember.
Do not commit private biographical details, contacts, schedules, addresses, health data, or raw chat logs.

Example:

The assistant should preserve uncertainty: if it does not know whether an important private signal is current, it should mark the signal as unknown and ask at a natural time rather than guessing.

The real profile can define private preferences, but those details belong only in `local-only/assistant/profile.md`.
